# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide demonstrates a minimal working example of the `qiskit-addon-sqd` package. We use sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) to refine noisy samples taken from a quantum circuit that approximates the ground state of a chemistry Hamiltonian. Ground state energies are approximated by diagonalizing the Hamiltonian in subspaces formed by the refined samples.\n"
msgstr "Panduan ini menunjukkan contoh minimal yang berjalan dari paket `qiskit-addon-sqd`. Kita memakai sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD) untuk memperbaiki sampel berderau yang diambil dari sebuah circuit kuantum yang mendekati ground state dari Hamiltonian kimia. Energi ground state diaproksimasi dengan mendiagonalisasi Hamiltonian di subruang yang dibentuk oleh sampel yang sudah diperbaiki.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more explanatory end-to-end workflows that run on quantum hardware, check out the tutorials:\n"
msgstr "Untuk alur kerja end-to-end yang lebih lengkap penjelasannya dan berjalan di hardware kuantum, lihat tutorial berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Sample-based quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization): chemistry Hamiltonian workflow\n"
msgstr "[Sample-based quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization): alur kerja Hamiltonian kimia\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization): fermionic lattice model workflow\n"
msgstr "[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization): alur kerja model kisi fermionik\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Prepare the inputs for SQD {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-sqd}"
msgstr "1. Siapkan input untuk SQD {#1-prepare-the-inputs-for-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, we define the chemistry Hamiltonian and quantum circuit that approximates its ground state. The system studied in this example is N₂ at equilibrium geometry in STO-3G basis with two core orbitals frozen. This system has ``8`` spatial orbitals and ``10`` electrons, which means the quantum circuit is defined on ``16`` qubits, where qubits ``0-7`` represent spin-up orbitals and qubits ``8-15`` represent spin-down orbitals. Since this is a closed-shell system with ``10`` electrons, we know each physically-valid sample should have hamming weight ``10``, where the hamming weight of both the left and right halves of the bitstring is ``5``.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, kita definisikan Hamiltonian kimia dan circuit kuantum yang mendekati ground state-nya. Sistem yang dipelajari dalam contoh ini adalah N₂ pada geometri kesetimbangan dengan basis STO-3G dan dua orbital inti dibekukan. Sistem ini punya ``8`` orbital spasial dan ``10`` elektron, artinya circuit kuantum didefinisikan pada ``16`` qubit, di mana qubit ``0-7`` mewakili orbital spin-up dan qubit ``8-15`` mewakili orbital spin-down. Karena ini sistem closed-shell dengan ``10`` elektron, kita tahu setiap sampel yang valid secara fisik harus punya hamming weight ``10``, di mana hamming weight untuk bagian kiri dan kanan bitstring masing-masing adalah ``5``.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Generate noisy samples {#2-generate-noisy-samples}"
msgstr "2. Hasilkan sampel berderau {#2-generate-noisy-samples}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a real workflow you would design an ansatz circuit, optimize it for hardware, and sample it on the QPU. Here we skip that and draw ``10,000`` uniformly random bitstrings instead. While our samples contain no information about the actual ground state, we will see that the SQD protocol can still recover the true ground state by iteratively refining these samples, diagonalizing, and using the energies at each iteration to inform the next round of bitstring refinement. We can eventually recover the exact ground state in this manner because the subspace containing the ground state is small enough to calculate exactly. Specifically, since we know each half of each bitstring (``8`` bits) should have hamming weight ``5``, we know the full Hilbert subspace of the system is size $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$.\n"
msgstr "Dalam alur kerja nyata, kamu akan merancang circuit ansatz, mengoptimalkannya untuk hardware, lalu mengambil sampelnya di QPU. Di sini kita lewati itu dan mengambil ``10,000`` bitstring acak seragam saja. Meski sampel kita tidak mengandung informasi apa pun tentang ground state sebenarnya, kita akan melihat bahwa protokol SQD tetap bisa memulihkan ground state yang benar dengan memperbaiki sampel ini secara iteratif, mendiagonalisasi, dan memakai energi di tiap iterasi untuk menentukan putaran perbaikan bitstring berikutnya. Kita bisa memulihkan ground state yang eksak dengan cara ini karena subruang yang memuat ground state cukup kecil untuk dihitung secara eksak. Secara spesifik, karena kita tahu setiap separuh dari tiap bitstring (``8`` bit) harus punya hamming weight ``5``, kita tahu subruang Hilbert penuh dari sistem ini berukuran $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Post-process with SQD {#3-post-process-with-sqd}"
msgstr "3. Pasca-proses dengan SQD {#3-post-process-with-sqd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The objective of the SQD algorithm is to refine noisy samples taken from a QPU and ultimately diagonalize the Hamiltonian in a subspace spanned by those refined samples. This is done iteratively as follows:\n"
msgstr "Tujuan algoritma SQD adalah memperbaiki sampel berderau yang diambil dari QPU dan akhirnya mendiagonalisasi Hamiltonian di subruang yang direntang oleh sampel yang sudah diperbaiki itu. Ini dilakukan secara iteratif sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refine samples by postselecting only those which have correct particle number for both the spin-up and spin-down subsystems\n"
msgstr "Perbaiki sampel dengan postselection, hanya mengambil yang punya jumlah partikel benar untuk subsistem spin-up maupun spin-down\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonalize in small subspaces spanned by the refined samples and collect information about the subspaces that yield the the best (lowest) energies.\n"
msgstr "Diagonalisasi di subruang kecil yang direntang oleh sampel yang sudah diperbaiki, lalu kumpulkan informasi tentang subruang yang menghasilkan energi terbaik (terendah).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each iteration:\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap iterasi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refine the noisy samples by probabilistically flipping bits in samples with incorrect particle number. The probabilities are calculated using the subspace information from the most recent diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Perbaiki sampel berderau dengan membalik bit secara probabilistik pada sampel yang jumlah partikelnya salah. Probabilitasnya dihitung dari informasi subruang hasil diagonalisasi terbaru.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonalize in small subspaces spanned by the refined samples\n"
msgstr "Diagonalisasi di subruang kecil yang direntang oleh sampel yang sudah diperbaiki\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect information about the subspaces yielding the best (lowest) energies\n"
msgstr "Kumpulkan informasi tentang subruang yang menghasilkan energi terbaik (terendah)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can see from the output that the algorithm converges to the exact ground state energy after ``6`` iterations and that the diagonalization is performed over the full Hilbert subspace of dimension $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$. Of course, diagonalizing over the full subspace is usually not feasible, and therefore, systems with ground states having sparse support are the most likely to benefit from subspace diagonalization techniques such as SQD.\n"
msgstr "Dari output terlihat bahwa algoritma konvergen ke energi ground state yang eksak setelah ``6`` iterasi dan diagonalisasi dilakukan pada seluruh subruang Hilbert berdimensi $\\binom{8}{5}^2=3136$. Tentu saja, mendiagonalisasi seluruh subruang biasanya tidak layak, sehingga sistem dengan ground state yang punya support jarang (sparse) paling mungkin diuntungkan oleh teknik diagonalisasi subruang seperti SQD.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more information on the diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian function, visit the [API docs](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian).\n"
msgstr "Untuk informasi lebih lanjut tentang fungsi diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian, kunjungi [dokumentasi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion#diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian).\n"
